      "text": "Two copper layers; through vias only. This layout does not verify circuit function.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-004",
      "text": "Common 3.3 V Feather interface aliases only. MCU GPIO mappings and analog capabilities depend on the actual Feather. FREE must not be assumed to be ground.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-005",
      "text": "Classic 2.0 × 0.9 inch footprint, 16 + 12 contacts, USB-left. Choose add-on for a FeatherWing or carrier to mount a Feather. Not a claim of universal board/circuit compatibility.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-006",
      "text": "Header mounting only: no castellated reflow pads, underside USB/battery/test contacts or debug connector are included.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-007",
      "text": "Nominal 1.0 mm connector drills / 1.8 mm pads are defaults. Check the actual mating connector, assembly tolerance and engagement length.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-008",
      "text": "Pin captions do not join nets. Confirm power direction, voltage and current limits; no supporting power circuitry is inserted.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-009",
      "text": "The host envelope and access areas are 2D references, not a collision-checked mechanical model. Print at 1:1 and verify against the purchased board before ordering.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-010",
      "text": "L.1–L.16 and U.1–U.12 are COPPERBENCH bank identifiers, not microcontroller pin numbers.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-011",
      "text": "FREE is explicitly variant-specific. Verify AREF, analog support, power behavior and bus usage on the selected Feather.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "feather-classic-carrier-a-012",
      "text": "Wireless Feathers need their own antenna guard: this common non-RF interface cannot predict every radio placement. Add a copper keepout for the exact host when needed.",
      "status": "open"
